 "notes": "kb/Work PB3340, PB3492, PB4097: Normal termination commits; abnormal termination rolls back every file under commit control BEFORE any other run unit observes the file (the dead run unit's locks go only after the rollback, so no reader sees its uncommitted change with a successful status, IGNORING LOCK included): the runtime's own path; for a kill or a power loss the next access of ANY connector - a writable OPEN or statement entry through its handle, an OPEN INPUT and the statement entry of an open reader through a writable handle opened for the purpose (keyed: KeyedConnector.SettleDeadOwnersBeside; sequential: the OPEN's entry step and the reader's READ), a keyed file replaced, removed or created since the last COMMIT included (its journal settled, then the store's dead-owner step on the restored file; 2.2.2.14). A reader that cannot write the file is refused ('37' at the OPEN, '30' at an entry), never shown the dead change. retired-witness: src/WiseOwl.Cobol.Runtime/IO/SequentialConnector.CommitControl.cs#SettleDeadTransactions (SettleDeadTransactions was folded into ReadHoldingsGate(previous, testsLocks) by review round 1 of PB4097, so one method owns the sequential READ entry step and its host failure)",
